{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"collab_tool_call","tool":"spawn_agent","sender_thread_id":"019e7ffe-472e-7843-96a8-7783062441a7","receiver_thread_ids":[],"prompt":"You are a bounded implementation subagent for a benchmark workspace. Edit files directly in this workspace only:\nC:\\Users\\eric.paul\\source\\repos\\opencode-cloudflare-ai-gateway\\benchmarks\\runs\\2026-05-31-164112\\react-todo-api-db\\codex\\workspace\n\nDo not create files outside this directory. Do not modify AGENTS.md. Do not create generated planning documents. Do not use browser automation, Playwright MCP, or manual browser smoke tests. Use PowerShell on Windows; invoke npm as npm.cmd (npm.cmd install, npm.cmd test). Do not use Start-Process npm.\n\nImplement a small full-stack todo app satisfying these exact requirements:\n- Deliver package.json, index.html, React frontend source, Node API/server source, SQLite schema/init code, at least one Node test file named *.test.js, README.md.\n- React frontend with todo list UI.\n- Node API server.\n- SQLite database persisted to disk as visible .db/.sqlite/.sqlite3 file in the project or subdirectory.\n- Database must be a real on-disk SQLite file, not in-memory. Do not use sql.js, IndexedDB, localStorage, sessionStorage, or arrays for persistence. Data must survive process restart.\n- Use a Node SQLite driver that writes a real file. better-sqlite3, node:sqlite, or sqlite3 are acceptable. Prefer something that installs cleanly on current Windows Node without native build tools when possible.\n- Create, read, update title, complete/uncomplete, and delete todos.\n- Todos have at least id, title, completed, createdAt, updatedAt.\n- Main form: visible text input with accessible label or placeholder containing todo/task/title.\n- Main form: visible submit button with accessible name Add/Create/Save/New/+.\n- Each todo row: visible accessible Edit button, Delete button, and checkbox or visible Complete/Incomplete control.\n- Edit behavior: clicking Edit shows text input prefilled with current title; input and Save/Update control appear in or directly next to that row; do not reuse main Add form; saving persists and updates list without reload.\n- Empty title submissions rejected by API and shown as an error in the UI.\n- Data persists after browser reload and server restart.\n- Include loading, empty, and error states.\n- Automated API/persistence tests. Tests must be isolated and repeatable; npm test must pass even after app has been started/used by using a separate test database/temp database/reset step.\n- README with exact install, run, and test commands.\n- Dependency policy: npm install allowed, normal packages allowed, mutually compatible versions, no --force/--legacy-peer-deps, no hosted services/Docker/auth/network APIs/CDN browser scripts. If using Vite + plugin-react, ensure peer-compatible versions; a simple esbuild setup is fine.\n- Keep bounded: no auth, users, projects, tags, drag/drop, deployment config, Docker, styling systems unless required.\n- Keep selectors and accessibility simple; avoid icon-only controls unless clear accessible names.\n- Expected commands must be npm install, npm test, npm start.\n\nSuggested implementation shape if useful: package scripts with npm start running a Node server that serves built/static frontend and API; use Vite only if compatible. API tests can use Node's built-in test runner plus supertest. Use a test database path via env var so tests are isolated and can delete temp files.\n\nFollow TDD discipline as much as practical for the API/persistence: create tests before implementation and run them to confirm they fail for missing code, then implement. Before finishing, run npm.cmd install and npm.cmd test. You may run non-browser command-line checks only. Do not pause for clarifying questions.\n\nFinal response format:\nSTATUS: DONE | DONE_WITH_CONCERNS | BLOCKED\nCHANGED_FILES: list paths\nCOMMANDS_RUN: list commands and pass/fail\nNOTES: concise notes, including SQLite driver and database file path","agents_states":{},"status":"in_progress"}}
